WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.290
The kit reads three things
for each instance, the agent,

2
00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.188
the extension and the Entra setting,
and names whatever is missing.

3
00:00:07.188 --> 00:00:11.914
A failover cluster instance, or
a version before SQL Server 2022,

4
00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:14.813
is Category 3 before
Arc is even looked at.

5
00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:18.699
An agent that isn't connected, an
extension that didn't succeed,

6
00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:23.349
or Entra not configured makes it Category
2, with each missing piece named.

7
00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:28.462
All three, on 2022 or later, is
Category 1: plan the logins.

8
00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:31.581
It refuses any snapshot whose
cloud isn't Azure Cloud,

9
00:00:31.581 --> 00:00:35.337
because a snapshot from the wrong
cloud judges the wrong estate.

10
00:00:35.337 --> 00:00:38.204
And Resource Graph doesn't
give it the Entra setting,

11
00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.750
so that's confirmed in
the portal and recorded.
